      <div class="scroll"><table><caption class="muted" style="text-align:left;padding:0 12px 10px">Covered areas under the 2025 RECA reauthorization</caption>
        <tr><th scope="row">Statewide</th><td class="covered">Utah &nbsp;·&nbsp; New Mexico &nbsp;·&nbsp; Idaho</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Arizona, these counties only</th><td class="covered">Coconino, Yavapai, Navajo, Apache, Gila, Mohave. <strong>Phoenix and Tucson are not covered.</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Nevada, these counties only</th><td class="covered">Eureka, Lander, Lincoln, Nye, White Pine, and part of Clark. <strong>Las Vegas is not covered.</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Manhattan Project waste</th><td class="covered">Parts of Missouri, Tennessee, Kentucky, Alaska</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Not covered</th><td class="covered"><strong>Montana, Colorado, and Guam are not in the current law.</strong> A bill to add them was introduced in July 2026 but has not passed. We will not tell you otherwise.</td></tr>
      </table></div>
      <p class="muted">Uranium miners, millers, and ore transporters are a separate category with its own rules, and are covered for lung and kidney conditions as well as cancer.</p>
